# apps/video: generated media. The video is rebuilt by `pnpm video:render`, which records the
# running app, speaks the script with Kokoro and renders — so none of this belongs in git.
# The poster frame is the one exception, because the README and the submission link to it.
apps/video/.venv/
# The HyperFrames CLI's own project state and render artefacts.
apps/video/.hyperframes/
apps/video/.narration/
apps/video/capture/
apps/video/assets/clips/
apps/video/assets/stills/
apps/video/assets/vo/
apps/video/assets/music/
apps/video/assets/audio/
apps/video/assets/master.mp4
apps/video/.render-tmp/
apps/video/renders/
apps/video/out/
!apps/video/out/poster.jpg

# The music bed. 3.3 MB, and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md records that this repository holds no
# licence, attribution or ID3 tags for it, so it is not ours to redistribute. The video that
# uses it is published; the track itself stays out of git.
assets/music.mp3
apps/video/assets/music.mp3
